{
  "info": {
    "name": "HackElite API",
    "_postman_id": "b7a3f1d2-6c1e-4f7a-9d55-hackelite0001",
    "description": "Health checks and the main HackElite endpoints, with test assertions on every request.\n\nSetup: import this collection and `HackElite.local.postman_environment.json`, then set `userEmail`/`userPassword` (any account) and `adminEmail`/`adminPassword` (an admin account) in the environment. `baseUrl` defaults to http://localhost:5050 (the API directly); use http://<LAN-IP>:5173 to go through the web dev server instead.\n\nRun order matters: \"1. Health\" needs nothing, \"2. Auth\" stores `userToken` and `adminToken`, and later folders use them. Use the Collection Runner (or `newman run`) to run everything.\n\nHealth only: run folder \"1. Health\". `/api/health` = the process is up (also reports `localDb`: false when the database is shared, e.g. Atlas). `/api/health/ready` = MongoDB is connected (503 otherwise).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5050"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Liveness: GET /api/health",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('responds within 3 s', () => pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(3000));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('ok is true', () => pm.expect(j.ok).to.eql(true));",
                  "pm.test('time is an ISO timestamp', () => pm.expect(new Date(j.time).toISOString()).to.eql(j.time));",
                  "pm.test('localDb is a boolean', () => pm.expect(j.localDb).to.be.a('boolean'));",
                  "pm.test('no secrets in the body', () => pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.match(/mongodb(\\+srv)?:\\/\\//));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "description": "Process is up. No auth. localDb tells you whether the database is on this machine.",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "health"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness: GET /api/health/ready",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('database is up', () => pm.expect(j.db).to.eql('up'));",
                  "pm.test('uptime is reported', () => pm.expect(j.uptimeSec).to.be.a('number'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "description": "MongoDB is connected. 503 when it is not.",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health/ready",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "health",
                "ready"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Public config: GET /api/auth/config",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "description": "",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/config",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "config"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Request id is echoed",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('x-request-id header present', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('x-request-id')).to.be.a('string'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "description": "",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "health"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
